[Music]  [Applause]  hello everyone  i'm pleased to take part in this  outstanding event and welcome all  participants of the ftth conference  to my deep regret i cannot participate  personally due to the hostile inhuman  and brutal russian invasion of my  country  before this terrible war  uk telecom at the leading and one of the  largest fixed telco in ukraine was fully  focused on bridging the digital divide  in our country  it was completely in line with our  president vladimir zelansky target  to make ukraine one of the world's  leading digital democracies during just  two and a half years  before the war our company  has successfully implemented several  large-scale fiber rollout projects  the key ones among them are gpon swap  projects  that are targeted to a legacy copper  infrastructure replacement  as a result our customers  have gained a new internet experience  while ultra-fast fiber connections  the second fundamental type of the  projects  are so called greenfield  ones that are devoted to g pawn rollout  where the fixed internet coverage wasn't  available at all  we expanded the geography of ftth  connectivity in all the regions of  ukraine  every year we build thousands of  kilometers of fiber optic lines and  bring connectivity to the millions of  ukrainians  in 2021  alone  we have built the records thirteen  thousand and seven hundred kilometers of  fiber optic lines  significantly extended our network  we went deep to the rural ukraine where  they  extended fiber broadband connectivity to  more than 500 small towns and villages  we have connected to fiber broadband  3.7 000 social infrastructure facilities  including nearly 600 medical offices and  800 schools  owing to luke's telecom  last year  160 communities have been covered by our  fiber network as a result of all  mentioned  we end up totally with 4.5 million  people  covered by our recently deployed fiber  optic network this is all  what i as a ceo of crypto.com would have  be happy to talk with you on such  occasion  before the february 24th  2022  as you are all aware in the early  morning hours of february the 24th we  found ourselves in the new reality of a  full-scale brutal war of russia against  ukraine  from that time the world's  critical national infrastructure have  gained the real  meaning for ukrainian  talkers  then then we have been seeking for an  answer to the same questions over and  over again  do we still have connectivity  are we going to stay connected  and the firm yes to both of them is now  absolutely vital to our victory  the critical part of ukrainian national  telecom infrastructure our network is  relied upon by the ukrainian military  forces our state agencies banks  operating businesses and all ukrainians  in raw time staying connected is a basic  human need and we feel our  responsibility to ensure it is satisfied  our sensitivity  to the absence of connection has grown  multiple  at this very moment  thousands of our employees together with  our colleagues from other talkers are  standing as  one  to keep our people  businesses  and institutions connected each day  our fellows heroes set off the damaged  network segments and repair cables in  blasting craters  sometimes under sounds of explosions and  gunfire  over into their work the critical  infrastructure of telecom and its  backbone network is in operation with 85  of regional nodes functioning  our employees have shown an undeniable  commitment to this mission  and i share one out of dozens examples  one of our network engineers in mikalive  region on the south of the country  whose house was destroyed by shelling  while he and his family were hiding in  the bomb shelter and right after he saw  the devastation caused by the enemy to  his own home  the first thing he did was to get to the  network node and start the digital  generator as soon as possible to power  equipment and let people  to connect with emergency services and  their families  one of the important thing we found out  during this terrible war time with the  unity among all key telcos in ukraine  at 5 00 a.m on february 24th  all of us became  one  no space left for words competition  market share  there were eliminated from our daily  corporate vocabulary we are all united  by one mission to keep our military  forces  social institutions and people connected  whatever it takes  i also would like to say that we have  not entered  this war unprepared in 2014  russia annexed crimea and started its  hybrid warfare in the donbass region in  eastern part of ukraine  this day was an opportunity to gain war  time management experience when we were  forced to reconfigurate our network  operation having lost chunks of  infrastructure to the raw dawn so-called  authorities of crimea donetsk and  lugansk  made us stop our business operations and  services  in the occupied territories later our  stolen equipment were used by the  pirates  internet service providers such as  phoenix  lugacon crimea telecom  today we face and witness even more  brutal behavior  in the beginning of may  russian troops destroyed the backbone  line on the south of the country and  re-ruled part of the internet traffic in  the occupied harrison region to the  russian managed infrastructure i am  absolutely sure it was not possible  without involvement of russian operators  owing to ukrainian armed forces we  managed to restore  our connection in the region the state  special communication service of ukraine  is appealing to the international  telecommunication unit regarding this  incident russian mobile operators  including ross telecom playing up to the  aggressive military goals of their  government  they openly violate the rules and  standards for interconnection and  traffic routing established by the itu  and the european regulators moreover the  russian operators brutally ignore the  rules for using ipx number resources set  for global internet services  all involved russian operators roughly  challenge  the entire global and european telecom  community  having experienced this challenge and  its destructive power  we at hookster.com are absolutely  convinced that there can be only one  response to such brutal elections  to impose the tough functions against  russian operators and their adulation  from the global telecom community even  more i strongly believe  we need to complete embargo on  commercial and technological relations  with these companies in opposite to our  attitude to russians we deeply  appreciate technical and humanitarian  aid of our european partners orange  polska british telecom global east  grotel and the rest are helping us to  withstand the unprovoked and equal  military aggression  at the representative of ukrainian telco  community  i deeply appreciate all the actions  taken by the international colleagues  at the european union body of european  regulators for electronic communications  the european commission and all the  other committed organizations yet i am  one again calling to all the decision  makers and the honorary guests to  consider any actions possible to  suppress the ability  of the aggressor to work in our common  telecom space  i urge colleagues to consider the  international embargo on russian telcos  who are behaving  just as military pirates on ukrainian  territory we must heavily protect our  common information space and isolate  european telcas community from piracy  and propaganda content of russian  operators  at the end of my speech i'd like to  state  that we continue to fight for our land  our future our opportunity to share  european values and common  communications  thank you so much for listening me  and i do believe that one of the next  ftth conferences will take place in kiev  after inevitable victory of ukraine  [Music]  you

